# The one ignore file every Prettier run names with --ignore-path. The
# format:check row reads this committed file to decide which files it checks.
# Each pattern is anchored at the root, so a file of the same name deeper in
# the tree is formatted.
#
# Written by release-please on every release. Its bullets are `*` and its
# version headers carry a blank line prettier would collapse, so formatting it
# turns each release into a failing check on main. The manifest is written on
# one line by the same tool.
/CHANGELOG.md
/.release-please-manifest.json

# Directories a checkout fills locally, which `bun run format` walks into,
# since --ignore-path keeps .gitignore from narrowing Prettier: build and test
# output, and Claude Code's worktrees, each a whole checkout of its own.
# Review refuses a file tracked under any of them.
/dist/
/coverage/
/.claude/worktrees/

# A contributor's own files, which .gitignore lists and `bun run format` would
# otherwise rewrite: lefthook's local configs and Claude Code's local settings.
# The gate refuses a tracked lefthook-local config, and review refuses the
# rest, with any path below one.
/lefthook-local
/lefthook-local.*
/.lefthook-local
/.lefthook-local.*
/.claude/settings.local.json

# This repository's own: the types file wrangler types generates, and the
# state directory wrangler dev and the test pool fill locally.
/worker-configuration.d.ts
/.wrangler/
